# Activity logs (capture hygiene)

Golden reference: `src/lib/activity-logs/redact.ts`, `http-capture.ts`, `sampling.ts`.

## Purpose

Persisted activity bodies are operator-visible in the support SPA. Mutations should send **partial** request bodies; high-PII success responses should be **enveloped** in the store; new sensitive fields must join redaction allowlists. Support UI contracts stay metadata-on-list / redacted-on-detail.

## Required patterns

| Concern | Rule |
| ------- | ---- |
| Mutation body | Prefer optional fields / partial PUT-PATCH semantics — do not require clients to resend the full resource to change one field |
| Response contract | Public API may still return full DTOs when product needs cache refresh; **activity store** must envelope high-PII 2xx paths (`isActivityEnvelopePath`) |
| New PII field | Add key to activity `PII_KEYS` (and secret sets if needed) + unit test in `src/lib/activity-logs/redact.test.ts` |
| Bulky nests | Prefer `OMITTED_OBJECT_KEYS` / compact — not a substitute for PII key redaction |
| Fail-open | Capture/writer failures must not fail user HTTP or background jobs |

## Good examples

```ts
// Partial write — only changed keys
await updateExample({ title: "New title" });

// After adding a PII field to the API, extend PII_KEYS and tests
```

## Bad examples

```ts
// Forcing full resource in every PUT body
// Persisting full auth 2xx DTO without envelope
// Relying on compactActivityJson alone to hide streetAddress
```

## Explicit prohibitions

- No logging cleartext passwords, tokens, OTP, account numbers, or personal contact fields in activity JSON.
- No requiring Discord posts from merge-readiness when touching these files.
- Do not fail-close the API if Timescale is down.

## AI guidance

Touching auth routes or `activity-logs/`? Check envelope list + `PII_KEYS`. Scheduled anomaly detection: `activity-logs-hunter` skill — do not invent tickets during normal feature work.
